{# Shared content + popover styles for home-gwern A/B/C variants.
   Wrapper pages set --gw-max / --gw-mx-l / --gw-mx-r and label themselves. #}

<style>
  .gwern-body {
    max-width: var(--gw-max, 38em);
    margin: 2rem var(--gw-mx-r, auto) 6rem var(--gw-mx-l, auto);
    padding-inline: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .gwern-body h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif, "Source Serif 4", Georgia, serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 0.2rem;
  }
  .gwern-body .gwern-email {
    font-family: var(--mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .gwern-body p { line-height: 1.55; margin: 0 0 1.1em; hanging-punctuation: first last; }
  .gwern-body h2 {
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0.6rem;
    color: var(--ink, #2a2820);
  }

  .gwern-body .work-examples-heading { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .work-examples {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .work-examples li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
  }
  .work-examples li::before {
    content: "\2022";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
  }

  .places-work {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .places-work li { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .place-name {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .place-org {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
    font-size: 0.82em;
    line-height: 1.35;
    opacity: 0.68;
  }
  .gwern-body .home-background { margin-top: 1.8rem; }
  .gwern-body .home-background-line { display: block; }
  .gwern-body .home-background-line + .home-background-line { margin-top: 0.55rem; }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .gwern-body { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  }
</style>

<article class="gwern-body" id="main">

  <h1>Lee Wilkers</h1>
  <p class="gwern-email"><a href="mailto:lee@leewilkers.com">lee@leewilkers.com</a></p>

  <h2>About</h2>
  <p>Hi, I&rsquo;m Lee. I do qualitative research, strategy, and design. I&rsquo;m based in Atlanta<span class="sn-marker" tabindex="0"><span class="sidenote-tooltip">The &ldquo;global health capital&rdquo; of the world &ndash; I&rsquo;ve worked with most major institutions in the area. <em>AKA</em>: city in a forest, hollywood of the south, the A, Hotlanta.<br><em>AUTBKA</em>: Terminus, 1830s &ndash; southern endpoint of the Western &amp; Atlantic Railroad.</span></span>, by way of the DC area<span class="sn-marker" tabindex="0"><span class="sidenote-tooltip">The data center capital of the world. DC stands for data center now if you didn&rsquo;t know.</span></span> &ndash; closer to cattle than the Capitol.</p>

  <h2 class="work-examples-heading">Some things I&rsquo;ve worked on</h2>
  <ul class="work-examples">
    <li>public engagement around contested technologies</li>
    <li>care systems for survivors of intimate partner violence</li>
    <li>organizational learning in disease-control campaigns</li>
    <li>campaign effectiveness beyond &ldquo;coverage&rdquo;</li>
    <li>microbial ecology and life-support systems for spaceflight</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Places I&rsquo;ve worked</h2>
  <ul class="places-work">
    <li><span class="place-name">Focus Area on Compassion &amp; Ethics (FACE)</span><span class="place-org">The Task Force for Global Health</span></li>
    <li><span class="place-name">Evans Research Group (Intimate Partner Violence)</span><span class="place-org">Rollins School of Public Health, Emory University</span></li>
    <li><span class="place-name">Human Engagement Learning Platform (HELP)</span><span class="place-org">Rollins School of Public Health, Emory University</span></li>
    <li><span class="place-name">Franklin Microbial Ecology Lab</span><span class="place-org">Virginia Commonwealth University, Richmond, VA</span></li>
  </ul>

  <p class="home-background">
    <span class="home-background-line">I studied biology and ecology at Virginia Commonwealth University in Richmond, along the James River.</span>
    <span class="home-background-line">Later, I got my MPH in global health at Emory&rsquo;s Rollins School of Public Health.</span>
  </p>

</article>
